<section class="about">
    <h1>About Me</h1>
    <p>I’m currently studying Computing and Informatics at Drexel University and working in cybersecurity. Outside of all that, I’m really into <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/app/266840/Age_of_Mythology_Extended_Edition/" target="_blank">strategy games,</a> <a href="https://www.nps.gov/appa/index.htm" target="_blank">hiking,</a> and making traditional woodblock prints. I enjoy spending time with my family, trying out new places to eat, and finding ways to be creative whenever I can. I’m curious by nature, always looking to learn something new, and I try to keep things real, whether I’m solving a complex problem or just enjoying a quiet moment.</p>
    <h2>My Hobbies</h2>
    <section class="gallery">
        <div class="gallery-item">
            <img src="\deploy\img\about\woodblock_station.jpg" alt="woodblock print station">
            <figcaption>My work station where I create my woodblock prints.</figcaption>
            <p>Woodblock printing is a traditional art where you carve a design into a block of wood. Then you roll ink onto the carved surface and press it onto paper to make a print. Each color usually needs its own carved block.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="gallery-item">
            <img src="\deploy\img\about\wood_prints.jpg" alt="woodblock_prints">
            <figcaption>This work was done in Japan by a small woodblock print shop called <a href="https://mokuhankan.com/" target="_blank">Mokuhankan.</a></figcaption>
            <p>David Bull is the owner of Mokuhankan and is an inspiration of mine when I look to carve art pieces.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="gallery-item">
            <img src="\deploy\img\about\hobby_hiking.jfif" alt="hiking_appalachian">
            <p>I have hiked on a part of the Appalacian Trail called Sunfish Pond. It is the southernmost glacial lake on the trail!</p>
        </div>
    </section>
</section>